the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    Income tax applies holds for *a case*.
    Income exceeds basic allowance holds for *a case*; open textured.
    Unlimited tax liability holds for *a case*; open textured.

the knowledge base r3_7_income_tax_law includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/income-tax-law.ruml".

estg 32a is published at "/akn/de/act/2024-01-01/estg#sec_32a".

estg 1 is published at "/akn/de/act/2024-01-01/estg#sec_1".

rule node_1 with provenance estg 32a:
Income tax applies holds for a case if
    Income exceeds basic allowance holds for the case
    and Unlimited tax liability holds for the case.

scenario generated_1 is, as stated in "income-tax-law.ruml" at generated_1:
    % no data
    node_1 expects answers ["Income tax applies holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Income tax applies holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    node_2 expects answers ["Income exceeds basic allowance holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_2 expects answers ["it is not the case that Income exceeds basic allowance holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    node_3 expects answers ["Unlimited tax liability holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_3 expects answers ["it is not the case that Unlimited tax liability holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.

query node_1 is:
    Income tax applies holds for case 1.

query not_node_1 is:
    it is not the case that Income tax applies holds for case 1.

